 "origem": "autoral. Fatos: aço e concreto dilatam ~12 milionésimos por °C; 100 m com 50 °C de variação = ~6 cm; juntas de dedos e aparelhos de apoio https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Expansion_joint",
 "titulo": "Why bridges have a metal gap 🌉 #engineering #shorts",
 "capa": "THE GAP IS ON PURPOSE",
 "descripcion": "That thump-thump when you drive over a bridge is an expansion joint. Without it, summer heat would make the deck buckle or crack its supports.\n\nWhat should we explain next?\n\n#engineering #bridge #physics #howitworks #shorts",
 "tags": [
